Hi. DartR is awesome. Keep up the good work.<br><br>However, I&#39;ve found that the gl2vcf() function which worked previously on v2.0.4 is not working as before with v2.7.2 or &#39;flavour=dev&#39; (v2.9.?).<br><br>I&#39;m converting dartr created genlight (gl) to VCF and previously the gl@chromosome names would be exported to the VCF file (see screen shot and code below). However, this has stopped working.<br><br>I&#39;ve tested with gl&#39;s created with dartr V2.0.4, v2.7.2, and the dev version. All of them create a gl with gl@chromosome field populated correctly. I&#39;ve tested with several plink versions and plink_win64_20220402 works as expected with dartr v2.0.4 and producues a VCF with contig/chrom names populated appropriately (see attached pic left panel). When a gl is created with dartr v2.7.2 but then using gl2vcf() with v2.0.4 and plink_win64_20220402 this again works correctly. So its not dartr v2.7.2 upstream functions causing the problem.<br><br>However, using dartr 2.7.2 and the dev version with plink_win64_20220402, the chrom names are not transfered to the VCF. See the attached WinMere screenshot comparing two VCF files. On the left the contig &amp; chrom names are populated correctly (using v2.04. &amp; 

plink_win64_20220402). On the right the same fields are not populated correctly (using v2.72 and 

plink_win64_20220402).<br><div><br></div><div>Weirdly, even with v2.0.4 and two linux plink versions (plink_linux_x86_64_20220402 &amp; plink_linux_x86_64_20230116) I get the same problem.</div><div><br></div><div>I&#39;ll  continue using dartr v2.0.4 version until this is fixed but it would be great to have this working again in the new versions. I havent posted my raw data because I dont want it public but I can send it privately if you cant recreate the problem at your end.<br></div><div><br></div><div>Thanks for all the gerat work you do.</div><div><br></div><div>Cheers,</div><div>Dean</div><div><br></div><div>Code:</div><div>  gl2vcf(<br>    gl_test2,<br>    # Specify path to plink v1.9<br>    plink_path = &quot;I:/PLINK/plink_win64_20220402&quot;,<br>    outfile =&#39;test2&#39;,<br>    outpath = getwd(),<br>    snp_pos = &quot;0&quot;,<br>    snp_chr = &quot;0&quot;,<br>    chr_format = &quot;character&quot;,<br>    pos_cM = &quot;0&quot;,<br>    ID_dad = &quot;0&quot;,<br>    ID_mom = &quot;0&quot;,<br>    sex_code = &quot;unknown&quot;,<br>    phen_value = &quot;0&quot;,<br>    verbose = 5<br>  )<br></div><div><br></div>
